  "why_it_is_certain": "U+002D is not a Tibetan character. The 'g-y' in Wylie is a disambiguation marker separating a ga prefix from a ya root; it must not survive into Unicode. Illuminator writes these correctly. This project's own engine REFUSES the wylie outright: wylie_to_unicode('g-yas') returns the rule-3 flag, so whatever wrote these values was not it.",
